#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Makes the Art Loft pages faster on a phone: the print page stops downloading every size's picture, each print page preloads its first picture, the first cards load at once, and the hashed code files are cached for a year. Brings no change to the page markup, redirects or noindex setting. The new tests are only put in place if every edit succeeds. It does not touch the database.

Run it from the project folder, AFTER unzipping starscapes-page-speed-24oct.zip into it:   python3 tools/add-page-speed.py

What it does: it makes exact edits to 8 files and, only if all succeed, puts two new tests in place.
  scripts/dynamicPages.mjs, scripts/shareHead.mjs, src/artloft/CollectionPage.jsx, src/artloft/PrintCard.jsx, src/artloft/PrintPage.jsx, src/artloft/PrintsPage.jsx, test/print-pages-build.test.js, vercel.json

How it keeps you safe:
  - It checks ALL 8 files first. If any is not exactly the way it expects, it changes NOTHING and says which.
  - Before changing a file it keeps a copy, ending .before-page-speed.
  - It is safe to run twice: a file already done is left alone.
  - The new files (INSTALL-PAGE-SPEED.txt, tools/page-speed-files/test_page-speed.test.js.staged, tools/page-speed-files/test_print-page-pictures.test.jsx.staged) come in the zip itself.
"""
